    "status": "draft",
    "summary": "A piece of work has no declared answer to \"what must I have read before I act on this\", and no way to tell later whether that context changed. A ContextClosure is that answer as data: the specs, sections and obligations a task is answerable to, named by the task's owner. spec-spine resolves a closure request against the committed ledger and returns every member with its identity and one order-independent digest over all of them, so \"the context this work was done against has changed\" is one comparison. The closure lives in the consumer's record; spec-spine only resolves it, and no gate reads one.\n",
    "title": "A context closure is declared"
